&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:20px"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PDX Pop-Up Shop Owners Bring Forward Powerful Personal Stories and Creative Concepts in Downtown Portland Until December 24th&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color:#696969"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;From artists reviving 19th-century tintype photography, to a&amp;nbsp;glittering burlesque and boudoir parlor tapping into Old Town&rsquo;s vaudeville past, to an award-winning specialty bookstore focused on comics and graphic novels&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PORTLAND, Ore.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&mdash;December 2025&mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;As the 2025 PDX Pop-Up Shops continue&amp;nbsp;through December 24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;, the 11 participating small business owners are drawing growing interest for the distinct personal histories, cultural influences, and artistic disciplines they bring to their temporary storefronts downtown.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;Each entrepreneur&amp;nbsp;has navigated a unique journey to elevate their business, revitalize a vacant downtown&amp;nbsp;space, and&amp;nbsp;present a vibrant storefront&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&mdash;flipping neglected spots into inviting, one-of-a-kind shops in just weeks. From artists reviving 19th-century tintype photography, to a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;glittering burlesque and boudoir parlor tapping into Old Town&rsquo;s vaudeville past, to an award-winning specialty bookstore focused on comics and graphic novels, these shop owners are illustrating how creativity and resilience are helping to reenergize downtown.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;One of the Shops, &lt;strong&gt;Madam Cooper&rsquo;s Parlor,&lt;/strong&gt; has transformed a vacant Old Town space at Ankeny Alley to offer a particularly unique experience&mdash;a glittering&amp;nbsp;boutique with a miniature Music Box Theatre offering six-minute burlesque performances, often accompanied by a live piano player and a menu of Spanish Coffees and hot popcorn. Together with performer-led walking tours on Old Town&rsquo;s storied past, the Parlor is reminiscent of the historic Entertainment District, which housed&amp;nbsp;vaudeville houses, saloons, cabarets, and offbeat nightlife. Today, entrepreneurs like Madam Cooper are channeling that history to help revive the neighborhood&rsquo;s energy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&ldquo;Portland has long embraced the bold, the unusual, and the beautifully theatrical,&rdquo; says &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Madam Cooper&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;, the co-owner, concept creator, and one of the performers of Madam Cooper&rsquo;s Parlor&amp;nbsp;&ldquo;We wanted to create&amp;nbsp;a love letter to Old Town&rsquo;s entertainment history, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;omething intimate, fun, and deeply Portland.&rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;Many of the entrepreneurs have overcome meaningful barriers in their journeys, navigating the challenges of scaling home-based businesses, reviving historical art forms&amp;nbsp;for modern audiences, or taking bold steps to grow into&amp;nbsp;brick-and-mortar storefronts and the central city&amp;nbsp;for the first time. Their experiences reflect the momentum of Portland&rsquo;s downtown recovery and small business climate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Books with Pictures&lt;/strong&gt; has operated in Southeast Portland since 2016 but&amp;nbsp;joined this year&rsquo;s Pop-Ups program to explore the downtown retail climate. Recently &lt;strong&gt;voted&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; the best comics store in the world,&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Books with Pictures is known for redefining what a comics retailer can be&mdash;an&amp;nbsp;inviting space for nontraditional readers that champions&amp;nbsp;stories&amp;nbsp;by and about women, queer communities, people of color, and people with disabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring! Treats for Dogs&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is also introducing something entirely different to the city center: gourmet dog treats made with human-grade, organic, gluten-free, and low allergen ingredients. The team, who opened Oregon&rsquo;s &lt;strong&gt;first-ever food cart for dogs&lt;/strong&gt; in Southeast Portland, has built a following with whimsical creations such as pupcakes, puptarts, and empawnadas. Like Books with Pictures, they joined the Pop-Ups program as a strategic opportunity to explore the potential of a permanent presence in Portland&rsquo;s central city. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&ldquo;With the Pop-Up Shops underway, we&rsquo;re seeing just how much the stories behind these businesses resonate with the community,&rdquo; said &lt;strong&gt;Sydney Mead, Senior Director of Downtown Programs at Downtown Portland Clean and Safe.&lt;/strong&gt; &ldquo;These entrepreneurs aren&rsquo;t just filling storefronts, they&rsquo;re bringing forward the kind of creativity and dedication to Portland that makes downtown feel alive again.&rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;Media interested in arranging interviews, capturing on-site activity, or speaking directly with the business owners are encouraged to reach out for coordination.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="OutlineElement Ltr SCXW189162678 BCX0" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Web&amp;quot;, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profiles of each PDX Pop-Up Shop, including photos and background details, are available at:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class="Hyperlink SCXW189162678 BCX0" href="https://www.downtownfortheholidays.org/holiday-pop-ups-1" rel="noreferrer noopener" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; text-decoration-line: none;" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;downtownfortheholidays.org/holiday-pop-ups-1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:aptos,aptos_embeddedfont,aptos_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;strong style="font-family:arial,sans-serif"&gt;FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial,sans-serif"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;December 10, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

